Vaani runs entirely on your machine. It does not bundle model weights or datasets; the items below are
downloaded by setup.ps1 / evals.datasets.prepare / Ollama, or installed by pip, and keep their own licenses.

== Models used at runtime ==

NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 (speech recognition)
  Copyright (c) NVIDIA Corporation. Licensed under CC-BY-4.0
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ . Source model: https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3
  Vaani downloads the ONNX conversion by Ilya Stupakov (istupakov/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-onnx on Hugging Face,
  declared cc-by-4.0). Changes: converted to ONNX (and an int8 quantized variant); no retraining.

Silero VAD (voice activity detection)
  Copyright (c) Silero Team. MIT License. https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
  Vaani downloads the ONNX build istupakov/silero-vad-onnx (declared mit on Hugging Face).

Ollama cleanup model (optional, chosen by you)
  The model you set as [cleanup] llm_model is pulled by Ollama and is NOT covered by Vaani's license. Check
  its license before use. The default, gemma3:4b, is under the Gemma Terms of Use
  (https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms). Other models Vaani was evaluated with: llama3.2:3b (Llama 3.2
  Community License Agreement) and qwen2.5:7b (Apache License 2.0), as reported by `ollama show`.

== Libraries ==

onnx-asr (MIT), https://github.com/istupakov/onnx-asr: loads Parakeet and Silero VAD.
ONNX Runtime (MIT), https://onnxruntime.ai . NVIDIA CUDA / cuDNN runtime wheels pulled in by
  onnxruntime-gpu[cuda,cudnn] are under NVIDIA's own license terms.
keyboard (MIT), pyperclip (BSD), sounddevice (MIT), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause and others), Pillow (MIT-CMU).
pystray (LGPL-3.0), https://github.com/moses-palmer/pystray : used as an unmodified, separately installed
  library; it can be replaced by installing another version with pip.

The complete pinned dependency set is in requirements.lock; licenses are those declared by each package.

== Evaluation suite only (evals/, not needed to run Vaani) ==

Open ASR Leaderboard text normalizer (evals/normalizer/, vendored unmodified)
  Copyright The OpenAI team and The HuggingFace Team. Apache License 2.0 (evals/normalizer/LICENSE).
  https://github.com/huggingface/open_asr_leaderboard , derived from OpenAI Whisper's EnglishTextNormalizer.

Datasets (downloaded by evals.datasets.prepare; manifests and result files contain their reference
transcripts, so the CC-BY-4.0 attribution requirements apply):
  LibriSpeech test-clean / test-other: Panayotov, Chen, Povey, Khudanpur, "Librispeech: an ASR corpus based on
    public domain audio books", ICASSP 2015. CC-BY-4.0. https://www.openslr.org/12
  FLEURS: Conneau et al., "FLEURS: Few-shot Learning Evaluation of Universal Representations of Speech",
    2022. CC-BY-4.0. https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/fleurs
  Svarah: Javed et al., "Svarah: Evaluating English ASR Systems on Indian Accents", 2023. CC-BY-4.0.
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/ai4bharat/Svarah
  negatives (synthetic silence/noise) and safety prompts: generated by this repository.

Eval-only Python packages (requirements-eval.txt, requirements-whisper.txt) keep their own licenses. The
optional Whisper baseline (faster-whisper, CTranslate2) downloads mobiuslabsgmbh/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo,
a conversion of OpenAI Whisper large-v3-turbo. It is never shipped or enabled by default.
